.SH NAME
pm-delete - Delete a registered project and its artifacts


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpm delete <target> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete registry metadata, environment files, and optional workspace directories for a registered project. The \fI<target>\fP argument accepts either a registered project name or a filesystem path. Unless \fB--force\fP is provided, the command displays a themed confirmation prompt before removing anything. Use \fB--dry-run\fP to preview the planned artifacts without changes. When \fB--backup\fP is enabled the archive is written to \fB--backup-destination\fP, falling back to the configured backup directory or \fB~/.pm/backups\fP.

.SH EXAMPLES
.B pm delete sample-app
.PP
Remove registry metadata and environment files while keeping workspace contents.

.B pm delete sample-app --keep-files
.PP
Explicitly retain workspace files while clearing project metadata.

.B pm delete ~/work/sample-app --all --backup --backup-destination ~/archives/sample-app.zip
.PP
Remove every artifact for the project and store a backup archive at a custom location.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	Remove project metadata, env vars, and workspace files

.PP
\fB--backup\fP[=false]
	Create a backup archive before deleting

.PP
\fB--backup-destination\fP=""
	Custom destination for the backup archive

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Preview deletion steps without making changes

.PP
\fB--force\fP[=false]
	Skip confirmation prompt

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for delete

.PP
\fB--keep-files\fP[=false]
	Remove metadata but keep workspace files

.PP
\fB--only-env\fP[=false]
	Remove stored environment variables only


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
